---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Schedule from '../components/Schedule.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

/**
 * The dates page — the page of record for the club's dates (D218, built by D227's split; the only surface that
 * prints a date since D306).
 *
 * Why a page at all: the homepage used to print up to four rows, and `/events.ics` was the only other place
 * dates existed. That left the one question a newcomer actually has — "what else is coming?" — with one
 * answer: paste a URL into a calendar client. This page answers it in the browser, and it is what the
 * homepage's next-date card and the nav's `Schedule` label both point at.
 *
 * Why it is a page and not a homepage anchor: D117 is the rule that killed `Schedule` and `Members` from the
 * nav, because they targeted paths the build did not emit and rendered the 404. A nav label is a promise
 * about a path, so the path has to be a file. `prerender` makes that true in the most boring way —
 * `dist/client/dates/index.html` — which is also what makes `scripts/check-content.mjs`'s dead-path rule
 * recognise `/dates` as an emitted route (it reads routes off the build artifact rather than remembering
 * them), what puts it in the sitemap (`@astrojs/sitemap`), and what keeps it off Worker CPU.
 *
 * It renders `<Schedule />` with no `variant` and no `limit`: the full width, and the windowed list — the next
 * `HORIZON_WEEKS` weeks, at most `MAX_ROWS` rows, both from `src/lib/event-window.mjs` (D238). The rows come from
 * `upcoming()` -> `data/events.json` — the same source `/events.ics` and the homepage's date count read, so no two
 * surfaces can disagree about a date (D223). What is windowed is this page's length, never the feed: a subscriber
 * who follows `/events.ics` gets every date the organizer has made, however far out — which is why the page names
 * what it left out rather than letting the calendar look short.
 */
export const prerender = true;
---

<Layout title="Dates - Matheapolis, a Minneapolis math club" path="/dates">
  <main>
    <Schedule />
    {/* The sibling the window names but does not hold (D374) — **unlinked by D404, and the route noindexed**.
        Round-6 review (2026-11-16), `/dates`/Remove: "Never link to an empty shelf". @measured 2026-11-17
        against `data/events.json`: 8 rows, two of them dated before today (2026-11-07 and 2026-11-11), and
        both carry `status: CANCELLED` — so `isPast` in `src/lib/event-window.mjs` returns false for all of
        them and `/past` lists nothing today. What ships is therefore the shelf with no door to it,
        and `past.astro` carries the `noindex` the same letter asked for on the other half of the ruling.

        The deferral, with its trigger (D148's rule: a parking lot nobody can reconstruct is a lost item):
        the link comes back in this page's own copy the day `/past` holds **three completed meetings** —
        `pastWindow(publishableRows(snapshot.events).rows, todayIn()).total >= 3`, which is the number the
        page's own list prints. Until then the route stays **built** (D117: a path is a file, and nothing here
        names a path the build does not emit), it keeps its `data-surface="past-row"` contract, and
        `check:dated-surfaces` still rules it as a page that prints dates. D374's reasoning for a page at all
        is untouched; only the pointer into it left. The paragraph is deleted rather than reworded, because
        "looking for a date that has already passed?" is a pointer to a disappointment, and a question the
        page cannot answer with content is not a question to ask. */}
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
